<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ameixial</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1663">1663</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-restoration-war">Portuguese Restoration War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ameixial was fought on 8 June 1663 near Estremoz in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alentejo">Alentejo</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-restoration-war">Portuguese Restoration War</a>. A Portuguese army under the Count of Vila Flor, with the Count of Schomberg and English and French auxiliaries, defeated the Spanish army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-austria">Don John of Austria</a> the Younger and recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evora">Évora</a>. It ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s last serious attempt to reconquer Portugal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ameixial.jpg" alt="Battle of Ameixial" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalha_do_Ameixal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
